            <ArticleTitle>Journal Club: Exacerbation of headache during dihydroergotamine for chronic migraine does not alter outcome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e196-e198</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Transient headache exacerbation during IV dihydroergotamine (DHE) therapy of migraine may prompt clinicians to prematurely discontinue DHE therapy, potentially depriving patients of the full benefit of DHE infusion. In a recent Neurology® article, Eller et al. evaluated whether or not worsening headache during DHE infusion was associated with suboptimal medium-term headache outcomes.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2016 American Academy of Neurology.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
